@page "/about"

<PageTitle>About</PageTitle>

<h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">What is and is not here</h1>

<Tabs Class="mt-6 max-w-lg" Value="have">
    <TabsList>
        <TabsTrigger Value="have">Kept</TabsTrigger>
        <TabsTrigger Value="lost">Dropped</TabsTrigger>
    </TabsList>

    <TabsContent Value="have" Class="pt-4 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        The component layer: markup, shadcn's class strings, the tokens, the
        <code>data-slot</code> contract, the ARIA, and the client behaviour in
        <code>ui.js</code>.
    </TabsContent>

    <TabsContent Value="lost" Hidden Class="pt-4 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        Everything server-side. <code>up-target</code>, <code>up-validate</code>, the 422
        contract, layers, <code>up-poll</code>, <code>UpChrome</code>. A WebView has no server
        to swap fragments from, so forms are <code>EditForm</code> and navigation is Blazor's
        router.
    </TabsContent>
</Tabs>
